          <Strong>Part 2</Strong>
        </Number><Title>Equality: key concepts</Title><Chapter DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2010/15/part/2/chapter/1" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2010/15/part/2/chapter/1" NumberOfProvisions="9" id="part-2-chapter-1" RestrictStartDate="2013-06-25"><Number>Chapter 1</Number><Title>Protected characteristics</Title><P1group RestrictStartDate="2010-10-01"><Title>Sex</Title><P1 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2010/15/section/11" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2010/15/section/11" id="section-11"><Pnumber PuncAfter="">11</Pnumber><P1para><Text>In relation to the protected characteristic of sex—</Text><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2010/15/section/11/a" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2010/15/section/11/a" id="section-11-a"><Pnumber>a</Pnumber><P3para><Text>a reference to a person who has a particular protected characteristic is a reference to a man or to a woman;</Text></P3para></P3><P3 DocumentURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2010/15/section/11/b" IdURI="http://www.legislation.gov.uk/id/ukpga/2010/15/section/11/b" id="section-11-b"><Pnumber>b</Pnumber><P3para><Text>a reference to persons who share a protected characteristic is a reference to persons of the same sex.</Text></P3para></P3></P1para></P1></P1group></Chapter></Part></Body></Primary></Legislation>